            "detailed_description": "<strong>while True: learn()</strong> is a puzzle game about machine learning, neural networks, big data and AI. But most importantly, it's about understanding your cat.<br><br>You play as a coder who has just discovered that their cat is brilliant at machine learning but hopeless at human language. So it's up to you, with a little help from the cat, to figure out how machine learning works and build a cat-to-human translator, one puzzle at a time.<br><br>What you'll actually do:<br>- Build flowcharts from ready-made blocks: expert systems, decision trees, perceptrons, neural networks and more<br>- Sort data by shape and colour within limits on accuracy, speed and cost, then chase the gold medal<br>- Read the story behind every technique, with links to articles, videos and courses if you want to go deeper<br>- Take freelance jobs, buy better hardware, gamble on startups and dress up your cat<br>No coding experience required, and no code is written in the game. It's a first map of the field, not a course: you'll come out knowing what the words mean, what each idea is for and why it mattered.<br><br>Made for curious people who want to see how machine learning ideas fit together before (or instead of) a course, for parents and teachers introducing kids to logic, and for anyone who likes smart cats.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Meet the ideas behind machine learning</strong></h2><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/619150/extras/0cb96133bd63f99848408842677e7dbb.poster.avif?t=1790934846\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/619150/extras/0cb96133bd63f99848408842677e7dbb.webm?t=1790934846\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/619150/extras/0cb96133bd63f99848408842677e7dbb.mp4?t=1790934846\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br>Each puzzle introduces a real technique in the order it appeared in history: from the humble expert systems of the 1960s to recurrent neural networks that predict what comes next. A short note tells you what the block does in the game and what its real-world cousin does, and hand-picked links let you keep reading. Don't worry: it all plays out as a puzzle game.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Build it, run it, tune it</strong></h2><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/619150/extras/00b8a3671b7da3e9e68c41c6b3ce15fa.poster.avif?t=1790934846\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/619150/extras/00b8a3671b7da3e9e68c41c6b3ce15fa.webm?t=1790934846\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/619150/extras/00b8a3671b7da3e9e68c41c6b3ce15fa.mp4?t=1790934846\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br>Drag blocks onto the board, wire them up, press Release and watch the data flow. Bronze usually comes easy. Gold means finding a smarter scheme, trading a little accuracy for speed, or coming back with better hardware. A solution you're proud of can be saved and reused as a single block in later jobs.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Live the life of a freelance data scientist</strong></h2><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline crossorigin=\"anonymous\" poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/619150/extras/0b188412014c5cff1f1a0a3e1b683edd.poster.avif?t=1790934846\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/619150/extras/0b188412014c5cff1f1a0a3e1b683edd.mp4?t=1790934846\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br>Groundbreaking technology takes time, experience and money, so you'll pay your way as a freelancer. Read emails from very strange clients, pick contracts, sit alone in a dark room for days without saying a word, socialize on forums. That's what real data scientists do. We checked.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>From self-driving cars to startups</strong></h2><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/619150/extras/7418d2c7b927c40d86fd7472778ebc6d.poster.avif?t=1790934846\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/619150/extras/7418d2c7b927c40d86fd7472778ebc6d.webm?t=1790934846\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/619150/extras/7418d2c7b927c40d86fd7472778ebc6d.mp4?t=1790934846\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br>Jobs are inspired by problems machine learning has solved in real life, including a self-driving car with your cat as the pilot. When you feel confident, become the CTO of a startup: your schemes against the savage laws of the market. Cash out at the top and become a tech guru, or lose everything and crawl back to the doorstep of the HR department. At least it was worth trying, right?<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Improve your gear, improve your life!</strong></h2><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/619150/extras/9701782e467c9b9f7f34b431e2e0b5f6.poster.avif?t=1790934846\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/619150/extras/9701782e467c9b9f7f34b431e2e0b5f6.webm?t=1790934846\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/619150/extras/9701782e467c9b9f7f34b431e2e0b5f6.mp4?t=1790934846\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br>Once the money is flowing, buy hardware that runs your schemes faster. But it's not just about the hardware: get a new smartphone, a geeky figurine, fancy outfits for your cat. Hell, you can even buy yourself an aloe.<br><br><strong>Fun fact:</strong> this is more or less what machine learning specialists actually do. Now you can become one of them (minus the salary). <strong>while True: learn()</strong> is the best game about being a data scientist, because nobody else has been weird enough to make one.<br><br>Playable with a mouse alone or with a controller, including on Steam Deck. Available in more than 30 languages.",
